The claim that Φ(D) = Φ(D') is sufficient for relative isotopy is false in the stated generality (arbitrary compact surface, arbitrary cellular graph). The set of cells met does not record:
- how many times D crosses an edge or how many arcs it has in a face;
- the cyclic order of the crossings;
- the homotopy class of D on a surface of positive genus.
It is plausibly correct only in the pseudoline case. There D is a pseudoline extending the arrangement, so it meets each line once and meets each cell in a connected set. So an implicit hypothesis is missing.
